 \section{Conclusion}
-Dense ridge ranking leads tested predictors by mean AUC at both resolutions; incidence-gated models offer secondary support/stability trade-offs. The contribution combines a connectome incidence formulation, endpoint-sharing analysis, ranking/refit integration, and sparse-to-dense evaluation. The constituent tools and ridge reduction are established.
-
+Dense ridge ranking leads mean AUC across both resolutions and scopes. Cortical restriction generally lowers AUC and changes sparse-model rankings. Our contribution integrates connectome incidence, endpoint-sharing analysis, ranking/refit, and sparse-to-dense evaluation. The constituent tools and ridge reduction are established.
